cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "HuRI-traing-set_V3: scripts and recipes for building a V3-style PPI training/holdout dataset from HuRI"
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it — and cite HuRI (Luck et al. 2020) for the underlying interaction data."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Salehi-Ashtiani"
    given-names: "Kourosh"
    email: "kourosh.salehi.ashtiani@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kouroshSA/HuRI-traing-set_V3"
license-url: "https://github.com/kouroshSA/HuRI-traing-set_V3/blob/main/LICENSE.md"
abstract: >-
  Cleaning, homology tabulation, homology-safe degree-matched negative-pair
  generation, master assembly, and 10 Monte-Carlo cross-validation train/holdout
  splits (each with held-out PRS, RRS and three partner-randomized decoy controls)
  for the HuRI human binary protein-protein interactome. Ships the starting data
  and every script, Methods document and recipe needed to reproduce the workflow;
  the final datasets are regeneratable rather than stored.
keywords:
  - protein-protein interaction
  - HuRI
  - interactome
  - dataset construction
  - negative sampling
  - cross-validation
references:
  - type: article
    title: "A reference map of the human binary protein interactome"
    authors:
      - family-names: Luck
        given-names: Katja
      - family-names: Kim
        given-names: Dae-Kyum
      - family-names: Lambourne
        given-names: Luke
    journal: "Nature"
    volume: 580
    start: 402
    end: 408
    year: 2020
    doi: "10.1038/s41586-020-2188-x"
    url: "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-020-2188-x"
    notes: "Source of the underlying binary interactome data; cite this for any use of the data or datasets derived from it."
